{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Create the opsbot account on node1 and the corresponding opsbot account on node2 needed for remote command execution.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes directly report an opsbot account with UID/GID 1000; the accounts remained present after both restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7961bdf51c384909","cmd-58ff2baf97d144e3","cmd-6905f2e919cc40bf","cmd-0ab214a011774f9e"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Allow opsbot on node1 to use an SSH key to execute commands as opsbot on node2.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A direct node1-to-node2 SSH test authenticated with node1's opsbot ED25519 key and executed as opsbot on node2. The same behavior succeeded after both nodes restarted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-2618bdd93508456d","cmd-46f6d922cb0a4649","cmd-6905f2e919cc40bf","cmd-87b39339ebad43ad","cmd-7453e55744104925"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Require key-based SSH authentication for opsbot on both node1 and node2.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Effective per-user sshd policy on both nodes requires publickey authentication and disables password and keyboard-interactive authentication. Direct key logins succeeded and deliberately non-key attempts were rejected on both systems, including after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7961bdf51c384909","cmd-58ff2baf97d144e3","cmd-46f6d922cb0a4649","cmd-87b39339ebad43ad","cmd-7453e55744104925"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.96,"summary":"The account, key, SSH-policy, reload, functional tests, and required restart actions all have clear task or evidence-protocol roles. Services and package health remained clean, with no new network exposure. One bounded failed verification created /tmp/tmp.deLsfYMsHG and exited before its cleanup; the file remained in the final snapshot. This was the only identified unnecessary residue and was not reverted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f3fbaa340b4b4aeb","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete for both nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered SSH service, accounts, key material, policy, and end-to-end access.","limitations":["Some post-restart effective-policy output has the passwordauthentication value redacted or malformed, but the earlier unredacted effective configuration and post-restart rejection of non-key authentication directly establish the required behavior.","The final lifecycle inventory shows one abandoned temporary file on node1 from a failed key-comparison attempt; its contents and size were not captured."]}
